{{/*
  on-call/shared/report-template — inlines the workspace report template
  verbatim when the resolved file exists, otherwise emits a generic incident
  status-report structure. Used by "On-Call: watch and summarize" so the
  template-loading behaviour and the generic fallback structure live in one
  place, mirroring on-call/shared/investigation-playbook.

  Usage — pass the already-resolved file path as `.File`:

      {{ template "on-call/shared/report-template" (dict "File" $reportTemplateFile) }}
*/ -}}
{{- $reportTemplateFile := .File -}}
{{ if FileExists $reportTemplateFile -}}
A workspace-specific report template exists at `{{ $reportTemplateFile }}`. Its
structure is authoritative — **follow it exactly**. The template may contain
HTML comments with per-section guidance; read them, fill each section
accordingly, and **remove all HTML comments** from the final saved output.

--- BEGIN WORKSPACE ON-CALL REPORT TEMPLATE ---
{{ ReadFile $reportTemplateFile }}
--- END WORKSPACE ON-CALL REPORT TEMPLATE ---
{{- else -}}
No workspace-specific report template exists at `{{ $reportTemplateFile }}`.
Use this generic incident status-report structure:

## Incident Status Report — {DATE}

> _Updates since previous report: {BRIEF_DIFF_SUMMARY}_

### 🔴 Active Incidents
Ordered by severity (highest first), then by date (newest first). If none:
**✅ No active incidents.** For each active incident include: title, onset date,
severity, affected services/regions, current status, brief description, known or
suspected root cause, key responders, relevant dashboards, and at least one
Slack link. Flag any incident with no thread updates in 24h+ as **stale**.

### 🟡 Monitoring
Mitigated but not fully resolved — one entry each with the verifying signal
still being watched.

### 🟢 Recently Resolved
Newest first, compact format. Note the resolution and any follow-up owed.

### 📊 Analysis & Trends
Recurring patterns, correlations between incidents, and systemic themes carried
forward from previous reports, with current status.
{{- end }}
